- op: discuss  # 3c84
  at: '2026-05-04T05:37:16Z'  # 3c84
  by: agent  # 3c84
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3c84
  clock: 6  # 3c84
  nonce: 3c84  # 3c84
  message: "**Addendum 2026-05-04**: forensic discovery extends the regression's scope.\n\nWhile completing the UAT campaign cleanup (interview-driven follow-ups on WI-pijal and WI-pudil), I attempted `tracker update WI-pudil --status wont_do` and got `error: No items match prefix: WI-pudil`. WI-pudil was one of the 8 items filed in the same batch where the three lost UPDATE ops occurred. The CLI had reported the new ID `WI-pudil-fadah-fizol-zapaj-fohih-jidiv-bubiz-puvok` at file time.\n\nVerification:\n\n- `tracker list --tier canonical` — not present\n- `tracker list --tier workspace` — not present\n- `tracker list --tier stealth` — not present\n- `ls .agent/tracker/.ops/` and `ls .agent/tracker-workspace/.ops/` — no `WI-pudil-*.ops` file on disk\n\nSo the silent-loss generalization is **boundary-adjacent ANY ops, not just UPDATE ops**. The original incident lost **4 of ~17 ops**: 3 UPDATEs (WI-kivut tag-remove, WI-zojid tag-remove, WI-sokaz parent-set) + 1 ADD (WI-pudil).\n\n## Why this matters for investigation\n\nUPDATE-loss is detectable by reading state back and comparing to your action log. ADD-loss is **silent and undetectable in the moment** — the CLI prints a fresh ID, but if you don't know that ID was supposed to exist, you'll never check for it. An agent that batches `tracker add` calls and references the printed IDs in subsequent operations will get downstream \"No items match prefix: ...\" errors only when those subsequent operations are issued; an agent that doesn't reference them again will never notice the loss at all.\n\nThis makes the failure mode **more dangerous** than the UPDATE-loss case, not less. If the rebase-restore is silently dropping the boundary-adjacent line of `.ops` for any op family, a busy session could be missing tracker items entirely with no in-session signal.\n\n## Practical impact in this campaign\n\nZero — WI-pudil's intended fate was `wont_do` anyway (we'd just decided to promote it to INV-zuhub-takaf-jupiz-kumoh-modon-ralul-vunob-hisop). End state with no WI-pudil and INV-zuhub present is exactly what the post-interview plan called for. The discovery is purely diagnostic value for this regression item.\n\n## Suggested instrumentation update\n\nThe investigation hooks listed in the original 2026-05-03 note should add: when reproducing, **assert presence of every ID printed by `tracker add` immediately after the failed-push branch**, in addition to checking that committed UPDATE ops survived. The 2026-03 fix (PR #1772) presumably preserved committed ops — the question is whether the boundary-adjacent line of `.ops` (across all op families) is what's getting lost during the rebase-restore."  # 3c84
